        "payload": "tree aee453ed425baf99c2462b5abe9ae2412689ad05\nparent bfb52b50f5b7655967b95f0129cea8caf4c97f7b\nauthor Peter Zafonte <pzafonte@pm.me> 1793708569 +0900\ncommitter Peter Zafonte <pzafonte@pm.me> 1794578549 +0900\n\nkernel: let callers create the block manager\n\nBlock storage was configured and read through the chainstate manager.\nAdd btck_BlockManagerOptions and btck_BlockManager, and pass the block\nmanager to btck_chainstate_manager_create, which keeps a shared\nreference, so either can be destroyed first. A block manager serves\none chainstate manager.\n\nbtck_block_read and btck_block_spent_outputs_read take the block\nmanager. Each options object takes the total database cache and uses\nits part. Wiping the block tree db also wipes the chainstate db.\n",
