      "body": "<!--e57a25ab6845829454e8d69fc972939a-->\n\nThe following sections might be updated with supplementary metadata relevant to reviewers and maintainers.\n\n<!--006a51241073e994b41acfe9ec718e94-->\n### External sites\n\n* Code coverage & benchmarks: https://corecheck.dev/bitcoin/bitcoin/pulls/36854\n* Ralph review <img src=https://review.fish.foo/assets/bitcoin/bitcoin/36854.png alt=\"Ralph review status\"> https://git.fish.foo/bitcoin/bitcoin/pulls/36854#author-ralph\n<!--021abf342d371248e50ceaed478a90ca-->\n### Reviews\nSee [the guideline](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#code-review) and [AI policy](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/master/doc/AI_POLICY.md) for information on the review process.\nA summary of reviews will appear here.\n<!--174a7506f384e20aa4161008e828411d-->\n### Conflicts\nReviewers, this pull request conflicts with the following ones:\n\n* [#36858](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36858) <sub><img src=\"https://drahtbot.space/ack_count/bitcoin/bitcoin/36858.svg\"></sub> (refactor: break the blockstorage/validation circular dependency by pzafonte)\n* [#36856](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36856) <sub><img src=\"https://drahtbot.space/ack_count/bitcoin/bitcoin/36856.svg\"></sub> (kernel: add manual pruning by pzafonte)\n* [#36743](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36743) <sub><img src=\"https://drahtbot.space/ack_count/bitcoin/bitcoin/36743.svg\"></sub> ([RFC] build: build with -Wmissing-declarations/prototypes by fanquake)\n* [#36738](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36738) <sub><img src=\"https://drahtbot.space/ack_count/bitcoin/bitcoin/36738.svg\"></sub> (refactor: move block writes and pruning into BlockManager by pzafonte)\n* [#36735](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36735) <sub><img src=\"https://drahtbot.space/ack_count/bitcoin/bitcoin/36735.svg\"></sub> (validation: delete pruned files after a failed flush by pzafonte)\n* [#36621](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36621) <sub><img src=\"https://drahtbot.space/ack_count/bitcoin/bitcoin/36621.svg\"></sub> (node: batch block file pruning in a single pass over block index by mutatrum)\n* [#36598](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36598) <sub><img src=\"https://drahtbot.space/ack_count/bitcoin/bitcoin/36598.svg\"></sub> ([Demo] validation: remove AssumeUTXO by l0rinc)\n* [#36167](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36167) <sub><img src=\"https://drahtbot.space/ack_count/bitcoin/bitcoin/36167.svg\"></sub> (build: Enable `-Wunused` by fanquake)\n* [#35557](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35557) <sub><img src=\"https://drahtbot.space/ack_count/bitcoin/bitcoin/35557.svg\"></sub> (kernel, validation: Add btck_chainstate_manager_set_clock_time by ryanofsky)\n* [#35187](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35187) <sub><img src=\"https://drahtbot.space/ack_count/bitcoin/bitcoin/35187.svg\"></sub> (kernel: Block validation without a complete UTXO set by sedited)\n* [#31260](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/31260) <sub><img src=\"https://drahtbot.space/ack_count/bitcoin/bitcoin/31260.svg\"></sub> (scripted-diff: Type-safe settings retrieval by ryanofsky)\n* [#26022](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/26022) <sub><img src=\"https://drahtbot.space/ack_count/bitcoin/bitcoin/26022.svg\"></sub> (Add util::ResultPtr class by ryanofsky)\n* [#25665](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/25665) <sub><img src=\"https://drahtbot.space/ack_count/bitcoin/bitcoin/25665.svg\"></sub> (refactor: Add util::Result failure types and ability to merge result values by ryanofsky)\n\nIf you consider this pull request important, please also help to review the conflicting pull requests. Ideally, start with the one that should be merged first.\n<!--5faf32d7da4f0f540f40219e4f7537a3-->\n### LLM Linter (✨ experimental)\n\n\n\nPossible places where comparison-specific test macros should replace generic comparisons:\n\n- `src/test/kernel/test_kernel.cpp`: `BOOST_CHECK_THROW(BlockManagerOptions(context, data_dir, blocks_dir), std::runtime_error)` → Prefer `BOOST_CHECK_EXCEPTION` with a `HasReason` predicate that checks the failure message.\n- `src/test/kernel/test_kernel.cpp`: `BOOST_CHECK_THROW(ChainstateManagerOptions(context, \"\"), std::runtime_error)` and the null-path equivalent → Prefer `BOOST_CHECK_EXCEPTION` with a `HasReason` predicate.\n- `src/test/kernel/test_kernel.cpp`: `BOOST_CHECK_THROW(ChainMan(context, chainman_opts, blockman), std::runtime_error)` for the context mismatch and already-used block manager → Prefer `BOOST_CHECK_EXCEPTION` with a `HasReason` predicate.\n- `src/test/kernel/test_kernel.cpp`: `BOOST_CHECK_THROW(blockman.ReadBlockSpentOutputs(tip), std::runtime_error)` → Prefer `BOOST_CHECK_EXCEPTION` with a `HasReason` predicate.\n\n\n\n<sup>2026-11-13 15:09:15</sup>\n",
